Hello list

First of all, thank you for all the interesting statistical discussions on this list!

And also, sorry that my question below will not be sexy and worse, not even dealing with statistics.

While preparing an aerial survey (with grouped data), we intend to use stems/streamers on the strut of the Cessna and our pilot is asking for examples of Supplemental Type Certificate (a document from aviation safety agencies) that would certify that the changes made in the struts (stems/streamers) meet the requirements for plane navigation/operation conditions. In short, this additional, though light, equipment on the struts/wings would require an additional certification paper of any of these kinds: STC - LSTC - FORM337 - LAISSER PASSER + additional elements to POH (Pilot Operating Handbook) detailing piloting limitation due to the stems/streamers.

My question to those of the list who sample distances from planes is thus: have you heard of these additional documents? For which plane and under which regime of certification or derogation (STC - LSTC - FORM337 - LAISSER PASSER)? Is it specifically for aerial line transects or distance sampling? Do you have copies of these documents? If yes, would you agree to send me a copy? Or if you do not have these documents, do you have any means of derogation or the likes? Or do you just do not care?

Thank you very much in advance for your help!

Best

Pierre

-------

Pierre Defos du Rau

